Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Setup Simulation that evolves through time with functioning rules. This would \
be scaling up the previous agent-environment framework from Sprint 1 and the \
ruleset.\
\>", "Subitem",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.93264082576614*^9, 3.9326408287651653`*^9}, {
  3.9782877671221943`*^9, 3.978287786493078*^9}, {3.9782879445852833`*^9, 
  3.978287944750145*^9}, {3.9782880657268734`*^9, 3.9782881296500435`*^9}, {
  3.978288788234421*^9, 3.978288800447117*^9}, {3.978527117173403*^9, 
  3.9785271617143*^9}, {3.978527238886692*^9, 
  3.9785272478974667`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"63893e4d-8b3c-8c48-9392-\
df5156d78766"],

Cell["\<\
The simulation evolving through time could look like this: 1) the simulation \
runs on discrete time-steps of 1s, 2) there are 60s in an in-simulation day, \
3) agents are free to move around in the simulation during a \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]day\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] but at the end of a day \
instantly get teleported back to a starting location in the simulation, after \
which the next day commences and they begin moving around again. Because of \
the nature of the simulation running on discrete timesteps of 1s, agents \
would have one action per second.\
\>", "Subsubitem",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.93264082576614*^9, 3.9326408287651653`*^9}, {
   3.9782877671221943`*^9, 3.978287786493078*^9}, {3.9782879445852833`*^9, 
   3.978287944750145*^9}, {3.9782880657268734`*^9, 3.9782881257603016`*^9}, {
   3.978289321282402*^9, 3.978289345370775*^9}, 3.97852715971517*^9, {
   3.9785272518462887`*^9, 3.978527255413315*^9}, {3.9785274008172894`*^9, 
   3.9785275329464455`*^9}, {3.9785276984677773`*^9, 
   3.9785277420017357`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1a0d8d77-bc3c-3942-bb14-\
cf3106720a08"],

Cell["\<\
Scaling up means extending the complexity of the ruleset, and increasing the \
amount of agents. Extending the complexity of the ruleset could be instead of \
making agents move around randomly, giving them a sensing distance and take \
shortest-paths to the nearest food.\
\>", "Subsubitem",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.93264082576614*^9, 3.9326408287651653`*^9}, {
   3.9782877671221943`*^9, 3.978287786493078*^9}, {3.9782879445852833`*^9, 
   3.978287944750145*^9}, {3.9782880657268734`*^9, 3.9782881257603016`*^9}, {
   3.978289321282402*^9, 3.978289345370775*^9}, 3.97852715971517*^9, {
   3.9785272518462887`*^9, 3.978527255413315*^9}, {3.9785274008172894`*^9, 
   3.978527412011612*^9}, {3.9785275410771656`*^9, 
   3.978527678767103*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"674f15a8-4c26-d344-adb7-\
21d9eb785f1b"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Setup parameter configuration.", "Subitem",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.93264082576614*^9, 3.9326408287651653`*^9}, {
  3.9782877671221943`*^9, 3.9782877843195724`*^9}, {3.97828810613875*^9, 
  3.9782881332940483`*^9}, {3.9782888025015087`*^9, 
  3.9782888465667706`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ab67b874-7563-1e44-8c47-\
f5fe4e29be82"],

Cell["\<\
All of us can suggest parameters and work on making parameters dynamic. I \
imagine that we\[CloseCurlyQuote]d have a multitude of parameters throughout \
our code: energy costs, movement speeds, food frequencies, etc. This would be \
creating the functionality for the user to change these parameters before and \
while using the model. I specifically imagine creating the functionality for \
a user to, for example, increase the food spawning frequency by 50% as the \
simulation is running. Before this functionality, we would just have a \
constant variable in our simulation: foodFrequency = 1;\
\>", "Subsubitem",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.93264082576614*^9, 3.9326408287651653`*^9}, {
  3.9782877671221943`*^9, 3.9782877843195724`*^9}, {3.97828810613875*^9, 
  3.9782881721289005`*^9}, {3.9782883130109577`*^9, 3.9782883135328426`*^9}, {
  3.9782883858539143`*^9, 3.9782884266582756`*^9}, {3.978288864431942*^9, 
  3.978288881114971*^9}, {3.97828891429858*^9, 3.9782889210029526`*^9}, {
  3.9782894490321026`*^9, 3.9782894490321026`*^9}, {3.9785272625103416`*^9, 
  3.9785273763441277`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"327d864b-d03d-394b-a280-\
dfcb36dc3b03"],

Cell["\<\
I hope to create this functionality for as many aspects of our simulation as \
we can.\
\>", "Subsubitem",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.93264082576614*^9, 3.9326408287651653`*^9}, {
   3.9782877671221943`*^9, 3.9782877843195724`*^9}, {3.97828810613875*^9, 
   3.9782881721289005`*^9}, {3.9782883130109577`*^9, 
   3.9782883135328426`*^9}, {3.9782883858539143`*^9, 
   3.9782884266582756`*^9}, {3.978288864431942*^9, 3.978288881114971*^9}, {
   3.97828891429858*^9, 3.9782889210029526`*^9}, {3.9782894490321026`*^9, 
   3.9782894490321026`*^9}, {3.9785272625103416`*^9, 3.978527390179508*^9}, 
   3.9785282316200123`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"3428f132-762e-d740-b114-\
22d19c1ae13f"]
}, Open  ]],

